course: dictionary
lesson: 15159
title: Scorching and other strong words
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Scorching is an adjective, a describing word. It tells you about a noun, like the day or the sun. Read the words around it: «It's scorching today!» The word today and the feeling of the sentence tell you it is very hot.
explain: Scorching can also describe speed or power. In football commentary, «a scorching shot» is a very hard, very fast kick. The clue is the sport: a shot is a kick at goal, so scorching here is about strength, not heat.
explain: Scorching has a plainer use too: it is the -ing form of scorch, which means burning the surface of something. A scorching sun can dry up the grass, which is one reason to wear a hat and use sun cream.
fact: Scorching means very, very hot (informal).
fact: «Scorching» can also mean very fast or very strong, as in «a scorching shot» in football.
fact: Scorching is the -ing form of scorch, which means burning the surface of something.
fact: «It's scorching today!» means the weather is extremely hot.
fact: On scorching days, wear a hat, drink water and use sun cream.
exercise: «It was a scorching day, so we went to the pool.» What does scorching mean here? | *Very, very hot | Very quiet | Very wet from rain | Very cold and icy
exercise: «The striker hit a scorching shot into the top corner.» What does scorching suggest about the shot? | Very wet and soft | Very slow and gentle | *Very hard and very fast | Very muddy
exercise: «The sun has been scorching the grass all week.» Which word is the -ing form of scorch? | grass | *scorching | sun | week
test: «The scorching sand burned my feet.» What does scorching mean in this sentence? | *Very, very hot | Very cold | Very soft and smooth | Very dark
test: «He hit a scorching drive down the line.» In sport, what does scorching mean here? | Very slow | *Very fast and very strong | Very sweet and sticky | Very wet
exam: «The scorching sun dried up the puddles.» Which word is closest in meaning to scorching here? | *Blazing | Freezing | Gentle | Damp
